        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: élever",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "élever — \"to bring up, to raise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ses grands-parents l'ont élevé à la campagne. His grandparents brought him up in the country."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Accent change: j'élève, nous élevons. Also to raise animals: élever des moutons."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "élever is built from é- and lever \"to raise\", which is inherited from Latin levāre \"to lift\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
